{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720042215","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237#issuecomment-6720042215","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1237","id":6720042215,"node_id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABkIu05w","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?u=4a54630ef210e4f76a452eea65cda1b56370734c&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-11-08T09:53:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:53:21Z","author_association":"MEMBER","body":"The current independent nominal-recipe review supports consolidating the JCM197/NBRC837/NBRC903 source proposals into one report-level ten-vitamin recipe. It identifies an additional authentic maintained comparator, `Mc_vitamins`, whose CultureBotHT Mixes block has the same ten numeric amounts after g-to-mg conversion. Existing-owner reuse versus a distinct material scope needs this concrete continuity assessment before installation. Missing D/DL specificity or added-water versus per-litre wording establishes neither identity nor difference. No second source-number owner is approved; all source and export holds remain.\n\nA confirmed existing component-reference defect is recorded here before correction as **SCI-TENVIT-003**: `data/ingredients/mapped/Mc_vitamins.yaml` components[6] names **calcium D,L-pantothenate**, consistent with primary CultureBotHT Mixes.csv row1122, but uses `CHEBI:31345`. The [primary ChEBI record](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:31345) has a stereospecific structure, D-calcium pantothenate synonyms and CAS137-08-6. That reference does not establish the explicitly D,L component. Preserve the literal source and exact quantity; select a child only with same-form evidence, otherwise withdraw the unsupported resolving reference. The new nominal JCM/NBRC candidates already keep calcium stereochemistry unresolved. This finding does not establish whole-stock identity, authorize a merge, or change role approval.\n\nThe root checked current GitHub search results for Mc_vitamins and pantothenate and the existing TV001–004 comments; this is an addition to the same bounded family issue, not a duplicate issue. The earlier NCMA-versus-CB attribution obligation and lipoic-acid catalog qualification remain explicitly inherited, rather than new blanket blockers.\n\nEvidence: `workers/w04/worktree/.temp/tenvit-nominal-reconciliation-independent-v1/` under the campaign root. Handoff SHA256 `40de7f6c1eca6d9084f510a534cf9b49b9fa03dea1806079b070289b9f81f515`; manifest `c963f7255725afedeaaf09037209591f6633efa4740e7afda9e9e60b0b689b7f` (all179 members rehashed by coordinator); final selector `dcdef5a08730540873425e3167d2495b2e50b76089c2772a5c4677852c25d870`. Actual primary/scientific, skeptical and final-assembly reviewer identities and scopes are retained. No maintained correction or release has been applied.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/comments/6720042215/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"pin":null}